cupid.description:
{green|Cupid}

Cupids are magically animated sculptures, much like Gargoyles and Golems. While the aristocracy indeed fancies them as guards of their estates, many Cupids are comissioned just to show off owner's wealth or serve as companions.

{gold|Special Ability : Flying. Gargoyle. Mind Immunity.}

{gold|Stack Experience:} Magic resistance increases by 3 percentage points per rank (up to 30%). Returns to its original hex after striking from rank 5 and prevents enemy retaliation from rank 8.

graniteCupid.description:
{green|Granite Cupid}

Cupids are magically animated sculptures, much like Gargoyles and Golems. While the aristocracy indeed fancies them as guards of their estates, many Cupids are comissioned just to show off owner's wealth or serve as companions. Despite their graceful movements, Granite Cupids' strikes are heavy enough to render their targets unconscious.

{gold|Special Ability : Flying. Gargoyle. Mind Immunity. 20% chance to cast Stun after attack}
Stunned creatures cannot act or retaliate for up to two turns; being attacked ends the stun. Undead, Gargoyle, Non-living and immune to mind creatures are immune to Stun attack.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Stun chance reaches 25/30/35/40% at ranks 3/5/7/9 (total chance, not added to the base 20%). Magic resistance reaches 5/10/15% at ranks 5/7/9.

homunculus.description:
{green|Homunculus}

Homunculi are more like animals than people. They are produced in a complex alchemical reaction and are small, disproportionate, yet strong caricatures of the proper human beings. They are usually tasked with works that need considerable strength, human-level agility and intelligence of a dog. Valuable asset on the battlefield since they regenerate wounds at impressive rate.

{gold|Special Ability : Regeneration}
Homunculus Regeneration enables the top creature of the stack to regain 7 health each combat round.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Regeneration restores 8–15 HP at ranks 1–8 and fully heals the wounded creature from rank 9; it never resurrects fallen creatures. Jousting from rank 4 (+5% damage per hex travelled); Defensive Stance from rank 6 (+5 Defense when defending). Chance to cast Disrupting Ray before an attack increases by 5 percentage points per rank, up to 50%.

gildedHomunculus.description:
{green|Gilded Homunculus}

Homunculi are more like animals than people. They are produced in a complex alchemical reaction and are small, disproportionate, yet strong caricatures of the proper human beings. They are usually tasked with works that need considerable strength, human-level agility and intelligence of a dog. Valuable asset on the battlefield since they not only regenerate wounds at impressive rate, the presence of Gilded Homunculi slightly amplifies power of damaging spells.

{gold|Special Ability : Regeneration. Damage spells power increasing}
Homunculus Regeneration enables the top creature of the stack to regain 10 health each combat round. Additionally, the presence in the hero's army increases the hero's spell damage by 15% for all magic schools (not Spell Power). Splitting the stack does not multiply this bonus.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Regeneration reaches 11/12/13/14/15 HP at ranks 2/4/6/8/10. Defensive Stance from rank 5 (+5 Defense when defending); melee damage reduction reaches 5/10/15/20% at ranks 3/5/7/9. Hero spell damage bonus remains 15%.

fireNewt.description:
{green|Salamander}

Salamander is a name applied to a wide range of non-elemental creatures originating from the Elemental Plane of Fire. Due to their elemental affinity they cannot be affected by fire spells. Thanks to that, many alchemists employ them to tend to furnaces or other works involving sustained exposition to fire or heat.

{gold|Special Ability : Immune to Fire}
Although Salamanders are immune to fire magic, they are not unaffected by fire-based creature attacks. For example Magogs' fireball attack or Dragons' breath attacks are not considered to be magical and therefore they do harm Salamanders.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Fire Shield reflects 5 percentage points more damage per rank, up to 50%. From rank 4, positive spells can bypass natural spell immunity (Receptive).

Innate and cast Fire Shield do not stack; the stronger effect applies. Nefefareen grants Receptive to both Salamanders and, while under an actual Fire Shield spell, +2 Speed, +2 minimum and maximum damage, at least 1 Morale and a 33% chance of Immolation after attacking.

