{gold|Special Ability : Fearless. Affected by permanent Slayer spell. Triple strike}
Dodos are immune to Fear and enchanted with Expert Slayer. They can attack three times per attack but they never retaliate to enemy attacks (this does not prevent enemies from retaliating). Grand Dodos reduce the morale of allied non-Dodo creatures by 1.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Ranged damage reduction reaches 10/15/20/25/30/35% at ranks 2/4/6/7/9/10. Attacks ignore 5/10/15/20% of enemy Defense at ranks 4/6/8/10. No resistance aura.

mandrake.description:
{green|Mandrake}

Mandrakes are violent and whimsical creatures, while at the same time highly cultured. Their singing voices can cause an agonizing death and to make things worse for their victims, they spread the vines around the battlefield to entangle anyone who dares approach them.

{gold|Special Ability : Summon Guardians}
At the beginning of each battle, Mandrakes summon guardians — Tangle Vines. Vines occupy accessible hexes surrounding the stack. Each summoned stack contains twice as many Vines as the summoning stack contains Mandrakes. But beware! At the beginning, the Tangle Vines block the Mandrakes, preventing them from moving. Mandrakes should be positioned wisely within the army (not in the corners) to keep as many free hexes as possible for vine summoning.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Enemy hero spells cost 1/2/3/4/5 extra mana from ranks 2/4/6/8/10 (only the strongest stack applies). From ranks 4/6/8/10, has a 20/30/40/50% chance to cast Basic Weakness after a melee attack. Blocks retaliation from rank 5, binds enemies after melee attacks from rank 7, and fully regenerates the surviving top creature at the start of its turn from rank 10.

Ophrys grants both Mandrakes +5 HP and both vine types +1 Speed and melee First Strike.

regalMandrake.description:
{green|Regal Mandrake}

