{gold|Stack Experience:}
Enemy hero spells cost 1/2/3 extra mana from ranks 3/6/10. Regrowth reaches Basic/Advanced/Expert at ranks 4/7/10; spell power per creature increases from 1 to 1.25/1.5/1.75/2 at ranks 3/5/7/9 (total rounded down). Six casts per battle; guardian count unchanged.

Ophrys grants both Mandrakes +5 HP and both vine types +1 Speed and melee First Strike.

jabberwock.description:
{green|Jabberwock}

Jabberwocks, despite their appearances, are not related to dragons. Those foul creatures dwell in corrupted caverns and terrorize every living being within their reach. Scarlet ones, with scales tinted by bloodshed, can decimate a numerous army in a single sweep of their claws. It is no surprise that the mere sight of these monsters can paralyze with fear.

{gold|Special Ability : Flying}
Jabberwocks are susceptible to Advanced and Expert Slayer (KING2).

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Physical damage reduction reaches 5/10/15/20/25/30/35% at ranks 2/4/6/7/8/9/10. Magic Resistance reaches 10/15/20/25/30/35% at ranks 3/5/7/8/9/10. Unlimited retaliations from rank 5. From rank 7, retaliates before enemy melee attacks when retaliation is possible. Regenerates up to 40/60/80 HP of the wounded creature each round at ranks 8/9/10 (does not resurrect).

monstrousJabberwock.description:
{green|Monstrous Jabberwock}

Jabberwocks, despite their appearances, are not related to dragons. Those foul creatures dwell in corrupted caverns and terrorize every living being within their reach. Scarlet ones, with scales tinted by bloodshed, can decimate a numerous army in a single sweep of their claws. It is no surprise that the mere sight of these monsters can paralyze with fear.

{gold|Special Ability : Flying. Fear. Destruction}
Monstrous Jabberwocks are susceptible to Advanced and Expert Slayer (KING2). Living enemy stacks have a 10% chance of losing their turn to Fear (subject to fear immunity); splitting Monstrous Jabberwocks into several stacks does not multiply this chance. Decimation has a 25% chance after an attack to kill 10% of the remaining creatures in the target stack, rounded down.

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Mind immunity from rank 3. Acid damage after attacks: 5/10/15/20/25% chance at ranks 1/4/6/8/10; deals 5/10/15/20/25/30 damage per creature at ranks 1/4/6/8/9/10.

tangleVine.description:
{green|Tangle Vine}

Traveling through various lands, one might sometimes encounter trembling ground from which mysterious vines emerge. These enigmatic plants can paralyze any creature, binding it firmly to the ground. They have no dwellings and cannot be recruited into an army. Although they are immune to mind spells, Mandrakes' magic can make them loyal servants in battle skirmishes.

{gold|Special Ability : Teleporting. No morale. Mind immunity. Casts Bind after attack}
Vines are unaffected by morale, meaning that their morale rating is always zero. Additionally they have 100% chance to cast Bind after attack (like Denroids).

{gold|Stack Experience:}
Immune to Jousting from rank 3 and to Slow from rank 5, if the stack has the required experience. Summoned stacks do not automatically gain these ranks.

